<div class="container-1">
    <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="700">
        <h1 class="container-1-header">ASLAR Logistics</h1>
    </div>
    <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="800">
        <div class="container-1-content">
            <p class="container-1-text">
                ASLAR Logistics is a small, family-owned delivery business based in Sumner, Washington. 
                Since starting with Amazon in 2018, we’ve proudly earned multiple awards for our 
                outstanding service. Our dedicated team loves what they do, and we’re passionate about 
                building a supportive team who go above and beyond.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="container-2">
    <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="800">
        <h1 class="container-2-header">What does a normal day look like?</h1>
    </div>
    <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="900">
        <p class="container-2-content">
            Your workday begins at 9:50 AM and lasts approximately 10 hours. You’ll be assigned a 
            delivery van equipped with a company-provided smartphone. Each day starts with a brief 
            safety meeting and announcements. Afterward, you’ll head to your van to load up with 
            Amazon packages. Smaller items are organized in totes, while larger packages, which 
            won’t fit in totes, will also be part of your load
            <br /><br />
            Our delivery area stretches from Federal Way in the west to Enumclaw in the east, 
            covering everything in between. One day, you might be delivering to bustling 
            commercial zones in Federal Way; the next, you could be out in rural Black Diamond. 
            Expect around 150 stops per shift. The number of packages varies depending on your 
            assigned route and how many packages are delivered per stop—delivering multiple 
            packages to a single location is common.
            <br /><br />
            The company-provided smartphone gives you access to all your route details. This 
            includes turn-by-turn directions (similar to Google Maps) for each stop, the 
            customer’s name and address, specific delivery instructions (like gate codes or 
            other unique details for that stop), and the number of packages assigned to each 
            delivery.
            <br /><br />
            At the end of your shift, you’ll refuel your van and return to the Amazon warehouse 
            to drop off empty totes and share feedback about your route. The final steps include 
            a van inspection, clearing out any trash, and parking it for the night.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="container-3">
    <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="800">
        <h1 class="container-3-header">Testimonies</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="testimony-container">
        <div class="testimony-1">
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="900">
                <img class="testimony-1-photo" src="/Recruiting Video and Photos/Karen.png" alt="" />
            </div>
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="1000">
                <p class="testimony-1-text">
                    You know its always who you work with and who you work for that makes it that much better.
                    That's what kept me here so long. Great team in general, its like a big family. -Karen
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="testimony-2">
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="950">
                <img src="/Recruiting Video and Photos/Glen.png" class="testimony-2-photo" alt="" />
            </div>
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="1050">
                <p class="testimony-2-text">
                    I can change my schedule around if I need to go to class or take care of my family. -Glen
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="testimony-3">
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="900">
                <img src="/Recruiting Video and Photos/Ashley.JPG" class="testimony-3-photo" alt="">
            </div>
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="1000">
                <p class="testimony-3-text">
                    The company and the people have here, its a great environment, a great group,
                    a great management and they treat us employees very well. -Ashley
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="testimony-4">
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="950">
                <img src="/Recruiting Video and Photos/Sannara.jpg"  class="testimony-4-photo" alt="" />
            </div>
            <div data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-duration="1050">
                <p class="testimony-4-text">
                    I love the team I work for. We have great team managers and associates that drive.
                    Everyone is always willing to help. -Sannara
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="https://unpkg.com/aos@2.3.1/dist/aos.js"></script>
<script type="module">
    AOS.init();

        import Swiper from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/swiper@11/swiper-bundle.min.mjs'
        var swiper = new Swiper('.swiper', {
            slidesPerView: 'auto',
            centeredSlides: true,
            spaceBetween: 50,
            grabCursor: true,
            autoHeight: true,
            centeredSlides: true,
            loop: true,
            effect: 'coverflow',
            coverflowEffect: {
            rotate: 0,
            stretch: 50,
            depth: 120,
            modifier: 1,
            },
            autoplay: {
            delay: 2500,
            disableOnInteraction: false,
            },
            pagination: {
            el: '.swiper-pagination',
            },
        });
</script>